  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis village with one combined statement set; treated as cash basis. Governmental: Total Governmental Funds column of the Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (p5). beginning_cash is the beginning fund balance 68,435 and ending_cash the ending fund balance 142,019 (the statement's roll-forward; the fund balance includes due-from-other-funds and treasurer balances, balance sheet cash is 315,951 on p4). Identity 68,435 + 161,811 - 88,227 = 142,019. The 'Change in fund's presentation' (975)/975 between General and Weston 150 funds nets to zero. 'Other general receipts' 35,089 split by fund column (General 2,433, Streets 299, Cemetery 400 = Miscellaneous 3,132 per p3; Keno 2,833; Weston 150 29,124). Business-type: Total Proprietary Funds column (p7), measure net position: 303,608 + 182,617 - 183,965 = 302,260; depreciation 21,466 is included as a disbursement; business-type reported totals are sums (printed separately as operating and nonoperating). No transfers shown. Balance sheet is the Statement of Net Position - Total column (p1): Invested in capital assets (10,504) value sits beside the Restricted heading in the layout and was assigned to the Invested row since the total ties (net position 444,279); due to/from other funds 408,816 are not eliminated in the total. Detail: the budget comparison schedule (pp8-9) is for all funds combined, so no fund-level schedule; 'Other local sources' 220,850 mixes governmental and utility receipts and was split into two lines (computed from p5/p7) with the Total receipts line 344,428 (governmental 161,811 + utility 182,617 + 32 interest... = 344,428). Budget-basis figures differ from the statements (e.g., beginning balance 379,061 vs 68,435 + 303,608 = 372,043; ending 467,311 vs 444,279; water debt service 11,739 vs bond interest 6,287; electricity/sewer/depreciation differences). Budget schedule beginning/ending balances not recorded. Read pages 1-9 of 9",
